
464:5. Code of the Witch of Justice: Even the Enemy's Justice Is Justice!
465:"Argh... Long, long ago,//n//nan evil witch was laid to rest on the outskirts of One Han City.//n//nHer lingering spirit turned into a phantom, forever searching for a way to achieve resurrection."
466:Yuzu
467:...One fateful day, the phantom stumbled upon an artifact and brought down a terrible hex upon the world.//nAny living creature touched by the cursed rain saw their spark of life slowly drain away...
468:Thankfully, the Witch of Justice and her three trusty companions stepped in just in time!
469:The defeated phantom is fleeing with its tail between its legs!//nOur mission, as the Squad of Justice, is to –
470:capture that wicked entity and ensure lasting peace for One Han City!
471:???
472:Trick or treat!
473:!
474:Little Girl
475:Haha! If we do this, does that mean we can catch the evil phantom?
476:Amusement Park - Halloween Grounds
478:Your smile is actually the most powerful spell of all. Here, have some candy!
479:Young Mother
480:Miyabi–!
481:Miyabi
482:Yay, Mommy found me!
483:Wonderful! Make sure you stick close to her so you don't wander off again, alright?
487:You're surprisingly natural with kids.
489:Achievement unlocked: Halloween Volunteer of the Night.
491:Still, I wonder if that fate-obsessed fraud is actually onto something. She swore the phantom was hiding right here, but I've already turned this whole amusement park upside down...
492:Waaah, Miss Witch!
494:I wanted to give you this jack-o'-lantern, but Mommy said it fell sick because it suddenly stopped glowing...
495:Don't worry! Th-there's nothing wrong with that – it adds to the spooky Halloween vibe...
496:Wait a second... {var:player_nickname}, this jack-o'-lantern carries a trace of that evil phantom!
497:player
498:Excuse me, do you remember where the lantern went dark?
500:Let me think... Just now, when I passed by the haunted house...//nOh, thank you both so much for taking care of Miyabi. I don't even know how to repay you!
501:Argh! This lantern is already the best gift ever! Thanks, little one, you just did the Witch of Justice a huge favor!
502:{var:player_nickname}, target locked on the haunted house! Squad of Justice, move out!
503:Visitor A
504:(Yawning) So boring... This haunted house isn't scary in the slightest.
505:Amusement Park - Haunted House
506:Visitor B
507:Right? I thought they'd put a little extra effort into Halloween...
508:Haunted House Staff
510:If ordinary people find it snooze-worthy, then this place will be child's play for the Witch of Justice!
511:See? Nothing scary at all –
512:Falling Spider Prop
513:Bzzt! Whirrr!
516:(Gently stroke her hair to calm her down)
517:I'm right here. Don't be scared.
518:I-I wasn't scared! I was just calling it out to warn you...
519:Still, a giant spider dropped out of nowhere just now... Why didn't anyone else even flinch?
520:Now that you mention it... those visitors ahead didn't even pause. It's as if they didn't care at all...
521:No, something is very wrong here.
522:(Sniffing) I knew it! The stench of the evil phantom...!
523:A haunted house that isn't scary, plus the presence of an evil phantom...
524:Could everyone's strange behavior be tied to that phantom?
526:I get it now! The phantom swallowed up everyone's fear, which is why this place feels so dull to them!
528:Mystery solved!
530:Then why did you get scared?
533:...
534:...Argh! That was a trick question! You set me up!
535:Whatever, that's beside the point!
537:Soft light radiates from her staff, sweeping across the entire building.
538:Visitors
539:...
540:AHHH! HOLY–!!!!
543:The stench is getting stronger... This way!
544:Amusement Park - Food Street
545:The food street is packed, yet the atmosphere is strangely subdued – almost eerily calm.
546:Customer at Popular Stall
547:(Muttering) I've been in line for an hour and haven't had a bite. Feeling dizzy and lightheaded... Guess I'm practically a ghost now. Talk about immersive Halloween vibes...
548:Customer at Roasted Sweet Potato Stall
549:(Biting into a blackened sweet potato) Huh, completely charred... Well, nom, nom, at least it's chewy.
550:Cotton Candy Vendor
551:(Monotone) Cotton candy isn't sweet at all. The recipe's a bust. Whatever – if it doesn't sell, it doesn't sell. I'll just call it paying for the experience.
552:This whole situation...
553:is way too peaceful, don't you think?
554:is getting seriously creepy.
555:Argh! So you noticed how bizarre this is too!
556:Argh! So you felt the danger lurking here too!
557:Look at that guy – his sweet potato is charred black, yet he doesn't even care how terrible it tastes! What if it gives him food poisoning?
559:Argh... Anger, sadness, discontent – these negative feelings serve a vital purpose.//nThey are signals telling us, "There's a baddie nearby!" or "This place needs justice!"
565:...Phew, looks like everyone's back to normal.
566:Argh! A noisy, lively crowd – that's what a real festival should feel like!
569:It led right here... Wait, why did the aura suddenly vanish?
570:Amusement Park - Parade Route
571:Staff
572:Oh no, what are we gonna do?! The parade float... the ghost...
575:Ah, that kind of ghost...
576:Just stand on the float and create some cute, magical moments for the kids!
577:Well... My Code doesn't say I have to accept every single request that comes my way. Can I pass on this one...?
578:Please don't! So many kids are looking forward to seeing the cute ghost...
579:I don't mind helping people find lost items or carry heavy stuff...
581:Relax. You're at your cutest when you're just being yourself.
582:Safeguarding the kids' smiles is a form of justice too, you know.
583:I-is that so...? Hmph...! Fine then, I suppose I can take on this request – just this once!
584:Argh-gh... My formidable majesty as the Witch of Justice is totally gone... That phony fortune-teller better never see me like this...
585:Those kids over there are already smiling at you.
586:(Straightening up)
587:...Hmph, alright, alright! Ghost of Justice, r-rolling out!
588:Standing on the parade float, Yuzu does her best to shower the kids with candy,//nall while keeping a watchful eye out for any sign of the phantom.
589:Yet by the time the float reaches the end of the route, it is still nowhere to be seen.//nWe are met only with the children's innocent laughter and cheering,//nleaving our sole lead dead in the water.
590:The carousel... the roller coaster... the graveyard... the haunted house... the food street... the parade...
591:A Quiet Corner of the Amusement Park
592:Impressive. The Witch of Justice came through for so many people today.
593:It's all in a day's work for me, but still...
594:We've scoured almost the entire park! And we haven't even caught a whiff of that phantom!
595:Is it really going to end up playing right into that phony fortune-teller's prophecy?
596:Still dwelling on what Kaavi said this afternoon?
597:So this is where the prophecy said the phantom would show up! Let's split up and hunt it down!
599:Kaavi
600:There is no need.//nThe threads of fate have already been spun. When midnight strikes, the fugitive will walk right into its cage on its own.
602:The tarot never lies. No such thing will come to pass.
603:Her way of doing things rubbed me the wrong way, which is why I insisted on striking out on my own.
604:But if all this searching turns up empty...
605:Keep up the hunt. We're bound to turn up something.
606:Maybe staking out the plaza would be more efficient at this point.
607:Don't lose heart. We already know what that phantom is after. It feeds on people's negative emotions to stay alive, so sticking to its trail will definitely yield better results.
608:That's true... So where would it go looking for bad vibes right about now?
609:Aside from the cotton candy vendor who messed up his recipe and the visitors disappointed by the haunted house, pretty much everyone at the park is having a blast on Halloween night, right?
610:Just a moment ago, its trail led straight to the parade.//nThat's supposed to be the happiest event in the whole park – there shouldn't be any "food" for it there. Why head in that direction?
611:...Maybe it intends to whip up its own "food"?
612:Whip it up...? Argh, this is where the crowd is thickest! If panic breaks out here, it'll have a never-ending buffet of fear...
613:Oh no! The floats are about to make their return run, and that's when the crowd peaks. {var:player_nickname}, we have to hurry!
614:Staff
616:Float Driver
617:Come to me... your fear... your anguish... All your negative emotions shall become my sustenance!
619:The parade float careens wildly toward the crowd!
622:Yuzu, look over there!
623:A shadowy figure, almost indistinguishable from the night, leaps nimbly across the banners and lanterns hanging above the crowd.
624:{var:player_nickname}, after it!!
625:Yuzu grabs my hand and pulls me into the sea of people –//n//ndodging past oncoming tourists...//n//nand slipping straight through a flaming hoop set up for an acrobatic show...
626:It went that way –
627:...Wait, isn't that Kaavi's fortune-telling booth up ahead?
628:Hold your steps, hurried traveler.
629:Amusement Park - Central Plaza
630:After waiting in line for so long, turning back now would be a dreadful waste of what fate has orchestrated.
631:Allow me to grant you a reading... The Tower, reversed. Heh, it seems blood and calamity await you tonight.
634:Eight spectral swords forged from starlight materialize out of thin air, forcing a dark shadow out of hiding and trapping it squarely within Kaavi's crystal ball!
635:Did... did it work?!
636:Crystal Ball
638:Inside the crystal ball, the shadow thrashes frantically.
639:How sturdy is that crystal ball of yours? It's looking pretty unstable...
640:BOOM!
641:Surrounding Visitors
643:Ugh... It's so cold... I want to go home...
645:Panic and aggression sweep through the crowd in an instant.//nSuddenly, the eyes of several bystanders go blank as an unnatural force takes hold of them.
646:Controlled Visitor
648:Quick! Get her, everyone!
650:The phantom feeds on negative emotions, and this entire illusion is sustained by all that negativity!
651:(Channeling mana to suppress the crystal ball) I see...
652:I've temporarily halted the illusion's spread. The crystal ball is its core – strike it with raw magical energy, shatter it, and the phantom will be destroyed.
653:Do it.
655:(Looking pale) ...Stop wasting time on futile attempts. Fate dictates that this is the most efficient solution.
656:Argh, here you go again... The word "fate" doesn't even exist in my Code of Justice!
657:...You spent the whole day running around the park, only to wind up right back here. Even your precious code is etched into the palm of fate.
658:...So what if it is? As long as I stay true to the justice in my heart, I'll make this so-called fate serve justice too!
659:I've upheld justice throughout the entire park today, and that means you're under my protection too, dummy fortune-teller!
660:Don't you dare think I'd ever turn my back on someone who needs my help!!
661:...Heh. So I'm under your umbrella of justice too...?
662:Even after all this time as an apprentice, you're still just a laughably naive, hopelessly stubborn little furball.
664:Phony fortune-teller, you never intended to merely contain the phantom in your crystal ball, did you? You must have a way to purify it afterward. Out with it!
665:...Very well. I do possess a purification spell.
666:However, the negative emotions of everyone inside this realm are constantly fueling it. It will continue feeding on those feelings and regenerating endlessly.
667:If we keep this stalemate going, it won't be long before my magic is completely drained, leaving us in a far worse predicament.
668:Argh, so it's a battle of attrition...
669:So the key is cutting off its supply.
671:But how do we turn everyone's mood around?
673:...Maybe it's not that complicated?
674:Do you have another brilliant idea, {var:player_nickname}?!
675:Your little ghost act put smiles on everyone's faces earlier.
676:What if we convince them that none of this is real danger – that it's all just a "special performance"?
677:...Oh! If they think it's all part of the show, they won't be frightened anymore! Let's give it a shot... Hey, phony fortune-teller!!
678:I hear you. I'll focus all my power on purifying the phantom. How much time I have depends entirely on you two.
679:Hmph... Just sit back and watch!
680:Dropping her protective barrier, Yuzu throws her arms wide to face the restless crowd.
684:(Eagerly awaiting applause) ...
685:Yawning Visitor
686:What a snoozefest... Just another tired ghost-busting cliché.
687:Impatient Visitor
688:What a joke. I just came to have fun – let us out of here!
689:Eye-Rolling Visitor
690:The practical effects are kinda neat, but that dialogue is straight out of a bargain bin!
691:H-how did it flop this hard?!
692:Crack–
693:Panicking Visitor
695:A surge of malicious energy ripples through the air.//nTendrils of pure malice rise from the crowd, coalescing into solid spikes that rain down on Kaavi's crystal ball!
697:C-come forth, my adorable familiars!
698:Red Panda Squad
701:The sudden arrival of the red pandas instantly takes the edge off the crowd's hostility.
702:Heh-heh, cuteness is justice!
703:Crackle-clack–
704:Controlled Visitors
706:I-I am NOT an evil witch!! {var:player_nickname}, what do we do?!
707:Forget the witch playbook. How about we tell our story?
708:Our... story?
709:Another wave of dark energy comes hurtling straight at us –
710:Watch out!
711:(Perfect time to grab their attention!)
712:(Pretend to be hit!)
713:Ngh...!
714:I stagger back a few steps and collapse at Yuzu's feet.
715:!!
716:...{var:player_nickname}!!
717:Yuzu drops to her knees and gathers me into her arms, her eyes instantly filling with tears.
718:The dramatic fall immediately grabs the onlookers' attention, and the entire audience falls silent.
719:(Quietly) ...Don't panic.
720:(Quietly) It's just a show. I'm fine.
721:(Quietly) ...You scared the life out of me!
722:(Quietly) We've got their full attention – now's our chance.
723:(Quietly) Keep going while we still have them.
725:(Quietly) Just speak from the heart.
726:(Quietly) Like when you played the little ghost.
728:(Quietly) Genuine feelings are what move people.
730:(Weakly open your eyes and gaze at Yuzu)
731:(Offer a faint smile and wipe the tears from the corners of her eyes)
732:I'm okay... After all, we're... partners... aren't we?
733:P-partners...
734:I used to think the Witch of Justice never needed human companions...
735:But ever since you came along... I realized... having you around isn't so bad after all...
736:And after everything we've been through... I haven't even properly thanked you.
737:Thanks for sticking by my side, {var:player_nickname}.
738:So, am I officially your partner now?
739:...Y-you don't have to spell it out like that! Just keep it to yourself!
740:Amused Visitor
742:Someone in the crowd chuckles at her flustered, blushing reaction, prompting a wave of warm, genuine laughter from the audience.
743:Now's our chance!
744:Right!
745:Helping me "struggle" back to my feet, she calls out to the crowd.
746:My partner has been struck down by a dark curse! I need your power to save them!
747:Touched Visitors
748:Tell us what to do!
749:The law of Halloween dictates: trick or treat! And right now, an "evil witch" is trying to play a wicked trick on my partner – it's her!
750:...?
751:(Quietly) Just play along!
752:(Deadpan) Heh... heh... heh. I am the legendary Evil Witch of Calamity. Give up. Your companion is doomed to an eternal nightmare...
753:I won't let you have your way!
755:Enthusiastic Visitors
756:Yeah!!
758:Little Boy
764:The crowd erupts into excitement as, one by one, the people she helped begin to share their stories.//nEach spoken word transforms into a speck of golden light, rising into the air until they merge into a brilliant river of stars, sweeping directly toward her!
765:Argh! Behold the power of justice!
766:Well played. The purification spell is almost ready...
768:As Kaavi channels gentle magic into the orb, Yuzu guides the surging joy toward it. The two forces intertwine, purging the phantom from the crystal ball. It tries to flee –
770:Fleeing Phantom
774:Visitor C
776:Visitor D
777:That mysterious fortune-teller vanished too... Part of the act, maybe?
778:Word of that night's "special performance" spread like wildfire,//n//ncementing itself as the park's most talked-about Halloween tale.
779:And so, the gloom hanging over One Han City was swept away once more through the combined efforts of the Witch of Justice and her partner.
780:Future adventures undoubtedly await, but tonight belongs to celebration.
781:Argh-argh! A resounding victory for justice!
782:Your search wasn't for nothing – you solved a ton of problems for the visitors along the way.
783:Still, Kaavi said the phantom would manifest in the central plaza at midnight, and we're getting close to the hour. Why don't we go take a look? Catching that phantom is our top priority, after all.
784:Argh... Now...? Fine. Since the trail has gone cold everywhere else, let's check it out.
785:We leave the parade route and head back toward the central plaza.
786:But only moments later, piercing screams and the screech of tires shatter the night!
787:It's coming from the parade!
788:Out of breath, we rush back to find the float crashed against the curb, surrounded by panicked onlookers.//nThe phantom is gone, but its sinister aura still hangs heavy in the air, stronger now that it has feasted on the crowd's fear.
790:Plaza Visitor
791:Ahhh! That evil fortune-teller has lost her mind! Run!
792:Was she the one behind all that freaky stuff?! The whole plaza just turned into some kind of graveyard and a creepy forest...!
793:We track Kaavi down in a quiet corner. She looks drained, the crystal ball in her hands cobwebbed with deep cracks.
794:...Argh! What happened here?!
795:Nothing out of the ordinary. The phantom has been reclaimed. Fate unfolded exactly as it was meant to.
796:...Fate?! You've been branded an evil fortune-teller!
797:News Report
798:BREAKING: A dangerous disturbance was reported during last night's Halloween festivities at One Han City Amusement Park. The suspect, an unholy fortune-teller, fled the scene. Investigations are currently underway...
799:Damn it!
800:Attention everyone! Our next objective is to restore her reputation!//nKaavi might be a phony fortune-teller, but she's not an evil one!
801:And so, a new mission for justice begins.//nI can already tell that clearing Kaavi's name is going to be far harder than catching a rogue phantom...
811:By the night spirits' blessing, let our stolen thrills return!
812:Nectar of life, awaken these dormant emotions!
814:...Heh, she is precisely the one I have been waiting for. Tarot - Eight of Swords: Array of Binding!
819:...Tarot - Ace of Cups: Fate's Cleansing!
820:You're not escaping! Light of life, banish the shadows!
821:A-argh! You bet!
822:Thank you for telling me the story, Miss Witch! I have a present for you too!
823:Huh? F-for me? N-no need – whoa, don't run so fast! Watch your step!
826:Argh?! What's wrong?
827:How come? We literally just updated all our props...
828:Aaaaaaargh!! GIANT SPIDER!!! BEGONE!!!!
829:...She actually lost it so bad her hair fluffed up?
831:Argh-argh! Ruining everyone's Halloween experience is unforgivable. Justice will be served!
832:Huh? Screams! Finally, real screams in my haunted house!
833:Piece of cake! Wait... The phantom's energy is moving toward the food street! {var:player_nickname}, after it!
834:And that cotton candy vendor! He messed up the recipe and couldn't care less! At this rate, his stall will go out of business!
835:The phantom drained all of that away! Thank goodness we noticed, or this entire street would be doomed!
836:(Snapping out of it) Oh gosh, why is this line still so long?! My legs are completely numb! But I'm not giving up – I'm eating this today no matter what!
837:(Suddenly jolting) No way! I can't let my Halloween cotton candy be a disaster! I'm fixing this recipe right now!
838:(Spitting out burnt pieces) Yuck! Are you selling roasted sweet potatoes or lumps of charcoal?!
839:...Huh? The phantom's trail...
840:It's heading that way – toward the parade floats!
841:Showing your true colors at last! Evil phantom!
842:A Few Hours Earlier - Central Plaza, Amusement Park
843:Argh? You mean we just sit here twiddling our thumbs until midnight?! What if it attacks visitors in the meantime?!
844:WHOA! What's happening?! The float's out of control!
845:...It's the phantom! It's possessing the driver!
846:Everyone, clear the way! Spirits of the wind, clear the haze from this lost soul's mind!
847:(Slamming on the brakes) Wh-what just happened to me?!
848:Hey! Watch out for that thing!
849:Hummm... hummm... hummm...
850:Huh...? Wh-where am I...? Is this place haunted?!
851:Hey, stop shoving! You looking for a fight?!
852:It's her! That fortune-teller did this! She's an evil witch!
853:Hold it right there! Rings of the ancient tree, raise a barrier and buy us some time!
854:...No way! You'll get hurt! You dummy, did you forget your magic is currently linked straight to that ball?! We need another plan!
855:Argh! I'm eighteen years old! Stop calling me that! And who are you calling naive–
856:Argh! That's it! If we can stop everyone from being scared and get them smiling instead, it won't be able to recover!
857:Ladies and gentlemen! Get ready for a special Halloween surprise – a grand showdown between the Witch of Justice and the Witch of Evil!
858:...Wait, what? This whole mess is just a show?
859:(Thrusting her staff into the air) Ahem! Hark, for I am the Witch of Justice, sent by divine decree!//nEverything you see before you is part of a grand spectacle staged to capture a wicked spirit that has eluded us for a thousand years!
860:Boring! Screw this! Fraud!
861:Shoot! It's harvesting everyone's frustration!
862:Argh-gh-gh–!
863:The Red Panda Squad bursts onto the scene in spectacular fashion, blocking every last attack!
864:Whoa! Red pandas! They're so cute!
865:Who cares if they're cute?! Let us go!//nYou're in cahoots with that wicked fortune-teller, aren't you! Trying to trap us here!//nWitch of Justice? More like Witch of Evil!
866:(Quietly) H-how am I supposed to act?! What do I even say?!
868:D-dummy! Who told you to jump in front of me like that?! I could've handled it on my own...
869:Pfft–
870:Everyone! Think of the happiest moment you've had tonight, and together, let's turn that joy into candy and drive this "evil witch" away!
871:Me! The cute little ghost on the float gave me candy today!
872:Me! I ate the sweetest cotton candy ever!
873:I-I found my daughter! We got separated earlier, and that witch onstage took care of her! Thank you so much!
874:And our haunted house! She's the one who brought it back to life!
875:Curse you... This isn't over... AGHHH!
876:Whoa, what a show!
877:Is it over already? I wanted more...
878:Coming here tonight was the best decision ever! Huh? Where did the Witch of Justice and her partner go?
879:Argh... Shoot! It got what it wanted! The trail leads straight to... the central plaza! It's heading right for Kaavi!
882:Hmph! Even during a top-secret mission, no incident is too small if it catches my eye – all must face justice!
883:That's it! Fear, anxiety, frustration... My spellbook says that a wounded phantom feeds on negative human emotions to regain its strength!
884:(Puffing out her chest) Because I'm the Witch of Justice! Weak phantom aura like this could never numb my feelings!
885:Huh? Oh, I meant we're one actor short for the cute ghost on our float! Could you step in and fill the spot?
886:B-but acting... cute? I don't even know where to start!!
887:I... I only know how to use magic to fight and purify... I've never even heard of "happiness magic" before.
